  "mapping": {
    "authored_date": "2026-07-18",
    "deviation_notes": "Trauma maps cleanly as a charge-stack accumulator (on-hit-dealt fill, cap 9) paired with hp_cost_scale self-damage — the exact 'more damage AND more self-harm per stack' coupling, both native. Drift: the identity's SOUL is the reset-cliff risk-management (ride toward 9, dread the 10th-stack reset, self-damage climbing quadratically 194*(N+1)); the engine accumulator caps-and-holds rather than modelling the overflow-reset threat, and hp_cost_scale 0.30 LOCKED clamps the escalating self-hit magnitude. Damage ramp intact; the knife-edge cap-tension is approximated.",
    "grade": "CLOSE",
    "kit_id": "poe1-boneshatter",
    "mapping_json": {
      "fidelity_notes": "Strong map: the Trauma mechanic is a charge-stack accumulator (sub_shape=accumulator, fill on-hit-dealt, cap 9) COUPLED to a self-damage cost (hp_cost_scale) — both native engine lanes, and their pairing is exactly the 'each stack = more damage AND more self-hit' identity. TEMPORAL_CHARGE routes the stack-engine-as-build-identity capstone; SACRIFICE_ASCENDANCY the self-damage-sustain trade (Untiring: regen scales with self-damage). THE DRIFT worth naming: the source's soul is the RESET-CLIFF risk dance — push to 9, avoid the 10th stack that resets, while per-stack self-damage climbs quadratically (194*(N+1)). Engine accumulator caps-and-holds at accumulator_max; it does not model 'overflow forces a reset AND the self-damage is a live threat you're managing toward the cap.' The damage ramp lands; the knife's-edge cap-management tension is a behavioral note the accumulator approximates. hp_cost_scale 0.30 LOCKED also clamps the top-end self-damage magnitude vs PoE's uncapped Trauma self-hit.",
      "motion_frame": "self-harm melee ramp: strike the pack, each hit stacks Trauma (more damage + escalating self-damage), ride the sustain against the climbing self-hit",
